<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Boundedness Analysis</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide formal boundedness proofs for both the traditional Scaling Metric and our proposed ARISE metric, demonstrating the fundamental differences in their mathematical properties.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Scaling Metric Bounds</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Scaling Metric <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Muennighoff et al., 2025</a>)</cite> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Scaling}=\frac{1}{\binom{|\mathcal{P}|}{2}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}p_{1},p_{2}\in\mathcal{P}\\
\mathcal{T}(p_{2})&gt;\mathcal{T}(p_{1})\end{subarray}}\frac{\mathcal{A}(p_{2})-\mathcal{A}(p_{1})}{\mathcal{T}(p_{2})-\mathcal{T}(p_{1})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Scaling</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Scaling}=\frac{1}{\binom{|\mathcal{P}|}{2}}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}p_{1},p_{2}\in\mathcal{P}\\
\mathcal{T}(p_{2})&gt;\mathcal{T}(p_{1})\end{subarray}}\frac{\mathcal{A}(p_{2})-\mathcal{A}(p_{1})}{\mathcal{T}(p_{2})-\mathcal{T}(p_{1})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Scaling Metric Bounds)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Scaling Metric is bounded: <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Scaling}\in\left[\frac{-1}{\delta_{\min}},\frac{1}{\delta_{\min}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Scaling</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Scaling}\in\left[\frac{-1}{\delta_{\min}},\frac{1}{\delta_{\min}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\min}=\min_{p_{1},p_{2}}(\mathcal{T}(p_{2})-\mathcal{T}(p_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\min}=\min_{p_{1},p_{2}}(\mathcal{T}(p_{2})-\mathcal{T}(p_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproof1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof 1</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproof1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any pair <math id="Thmproof1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{1},p_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{1},p_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmproof1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}(p_{2})&gt;\mathcal{T}(p_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}(p_{2})&gt;\mathcal{T}(p_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since <math id="Thmproof1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, the numerator satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1\leq\mathcal{A}(p_{2})-\mathcal{A}(p_{1})\leq 1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1\leq\mathcal{A}(p_{2})-\mathcal{A}(p_{1})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the denominator, by definition:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}(p_{2})-\mathcal{T}(p_{1})\geq\delta_{\min}&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}(p_{2})-\mathcal{T}(p_{1})\geq\delta_{\min}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Combining Equations <a href="#A1.E19" title="In Proof 1 ‣ A.1 Scaling Metric Bounds ‣ Appendix A Boundedness Analysis ‣ ARISE: An Adaptive Resolution-Aware Metric for Test-Time Scaling Evaluation in Large Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> and <a href="#A1.E20" title="In Proof 1 ‣ A.1 Scaling Metric Bounds ‣ Appendix A Boundedness Analysis ‣ ARISE: An Adaptive Resolution-Aware Metric for Test-Time Scaling Evaluation in Large Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{-1}{\delta_{\min}}\leq\frac{\mathcal{A}(p_{2})-\mathcal{A}(p_{1})}{\mathcal{T}(p_{2})-\mathcal{T}(p_{1})}\leq\frac{1}{\delta_{\min}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{-1}{\delta_{\min}}\leq\frac{\mathcal{A}(p_{2})-\mathcal{A}(p_{1})}{\mathcal{T}(p_{2})-\mathcal{T}(p_{1})}\leq\frac{1}{\delta_{\min}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since the Scaling Metric is an average over all pairs, it inherits these bounds. In practice, with normalized token differences where <math id="Thmproof1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\min}\to 1^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\min}\to 1^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain <math id="Thmproof1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Scaling Metric}\in(-1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Scaling Metric</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Scaling Metric}\in(-1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>ARISE Bounds</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For ARISE, we analyze bounds considering all possible accuracy transition patterns.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Sample-Level ARISE Bounds)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a single sample <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> scaling iterations, <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}_{i}\in(-\infty,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ARISE</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}_{i}\in(-\infty,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproof2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof 2</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproof2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">From Equation <a href="#S3.E5" title="In Sample-Level Awareness. ‣ 3.1 Metric Design ‣ 3 ARISE: Adaptive Resolution-Aware Metric ‣ ARISE: An Adaptive Resolution-Aware Metric for Test-Time Scaling Evaluation in Large Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, ARISE<sub id="Thmproof2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub"><span id="Thmproof2.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i</span></sub> is the sum of contributions from all transitions. Let <math id="Thmproof2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{I}=\{j:a_{i}^{(j)}=1,a_{i}^{(j-1)}=0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}=\{j:a_{i}^{(j)}=1,a_{i}^{(j-1)}=0\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote improvement transitions and <math id="Thmproof2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{j:a_{i}^{(j)}=0,a_{i}^{(j-1)}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{j:a_{i}^{(j)}=0,a_{i}^{(j-1)}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote degradation transitions.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}_{i}=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{I}}\frac{t_{i}^{(j-1)}}{t_{i}^{(j)}}-\sum_{j\in\mathcal{D}}\frac{t_{i}^{(j)}}{t_{i}^{(j-1)}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ARISE</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}_{i}=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{I}}\frac{t_{i}^{(j-1)}}{t_{i}^{(j)}}-\sum_{j\in\mathcal{D}}\frac{t_{i}^{(j)}}{t_{i}^{(j-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Upper bound:<span id="Thmproof2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The maximum occurs when there are only improvements and no degradations. The optimal accuracy sequence with a single transition at position <math id="Thmproof2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}_{i,\max}=\frac{t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}}{t_{i}^{(j^{*})}}&lt;1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ARISE</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}_{i,\max}=\frac{t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}}{t_{i}^{(j^{*})}}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As <math id="Thmproof2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{(j^{*})}\to t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{(j^{*})}\to t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, ARISE<math id="Thmproof2.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{i,\max}\to 1^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{i,\max}\to 1^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the supremum is 1.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Lower bound:<span id="Thmproof2.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The minimum occurs with only degradations and no improvements. The worst accuracy sequence with a single transition at position <math id="Thmproof2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}_{i,\min}=-\frac{t_{i}^{(j^{*})}}{t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}}&lt;-1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ARISE</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}_{i,\min}=-\frac{t_{i}^{(j^{*})}}{t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}}&lt;-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Since <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{(j^{*})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{(j^{*})}</annotation></semantics></math> can be arbitrarily larger than <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, ARISE<math id="Thmproof2.p8.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}_{i,\min}\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{i,\min}\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding intermediate values within <math id="Thmproof2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\infty,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\infty,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (ARISE Bounds)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The aggregate ARISE metric satisfies <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}\in(-\infty,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ARISE</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}\in(-\infty,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproof3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof 3</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproof3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">From Equation <a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.1 Metric Design ‣ 3 ARISE: Adaptive Resolution-Aware Metric ‣ ARISE: An Adaptive Resolution-Aware Metric for Test-Time Scaling Evaluation in Large Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, ARISE is the arithmetic mean of sample scores:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\text{ARISE}_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ARISE</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ARISE</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\text{ARISE}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">By Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Sample-Level ARISE Bounds) ‣ A.2 ARISE Bounds ‣ Appendix A Boundedness Analysis ‣ ARISE: An Adaptive Resolution-Aware Metric for Test-Time Scaling Evaluation in Large Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, each <math id="Thmproof3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}_{i}\in(-\infty,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ARISE</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}_{i}\in(-\infty,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Upper bound:<span id="Thmproof3.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> When all samples achieve the optimal pattern :</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}_{\max}=\lim_{t_{i}^{(j^{*})}\to t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}}{t_{i}^{(j^{*})}}&lt;1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ARISE</mtext><mi>max</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mfrac><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}_{\max}=\lim_{t_{i}^{(j^{*})}\to t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}}{t_{i}^{(j^{*})}}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproof3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproof3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Lower bound:<span id="Thmproof3.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> When all samples exhibit the worst pattern :</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}_{\min}=\lim_{r\to\infty}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(-r)=-\infty" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ARISE</mtext><mi>min</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}_{\min}=\lim_{r\to\infty}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(-r)=-\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproof3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproof3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproof3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\frac{t_{i}^{(j^{*})}}{t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\frac{t_{i}^{(j^{*})}}{t_{i}^{(j^{*}-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the token ratio. Thus, the range of the ARISE is <math id="Thmproof3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\infty,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\infty,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Algorithm</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present the complete algorithmic procedure for computing ARISE with adaptive sampling. Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix B Algorithm ‣ ARISE: An Adaptive Resolution-Aware Metric for Test-Time Scaling Evaluation in Large Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> outlines the main computation flow, while Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix B Algorithm ‣ ARISE: An Adaptive Resolution-Aware Metric for Test-Time Scaling Evaluation in Large Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> details the dynamic sampling strategy.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> ARISE Computation with Adaptive Sampling</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          Dataset <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, model <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, scaling iterations <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>, budget <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          ARISE score

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          Initialize <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>ARISE</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> For each sample
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}_{i}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>ARISE</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}_{i}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Scaling iterations
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
             // Adaptive sampling strategy

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*},a_{i}^{(j)},t_{i}^{(j)}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*},a_{i}^{(j)},t_{i}^{(j)}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AdaptiveSample</span>(<math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M},x_{i},j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M},x_{i},j</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
             // Compute contribution

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta a\leftarrow a_{i}^{(j)}-a_{i}^{(j-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta a\leftarrow a_{i}^{(j)}-a_{i}^{(j-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta a\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta a\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\leftarrow\left(\frac{t_{i}^{(j-1)}}{t_{i}^{(j)}}\right)^{\text{sign}(\Delta a)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>sign</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\leftarrow\left(\frac{t_{i}^{(j-1)}}{t_{i}^{(j)}}\right)^{\text{sign}(\Delta a)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
               <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}_{i}\leftarrow\text{ARISE}_{i}+\Delta a\cdot W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>ARISE</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>ARISE</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}_{i}\leftarrow\text{ARISE}_{i}+\Delta a\cdot W</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}\leftarrow\text{ARISE}+\text{ARISE}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>ARISE</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>ARISE</mtext><mo>+</mo><msub><mtext>ARISE</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}\leftarrow\text{ARISE}+\text{ARISE}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ARISE}/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>ARISE</mtext><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ARISE}/n</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Adaptive Sampling Strategy</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          Model <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, sample <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, iteration <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, threshold <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, max trials <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          Sample count <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, mean accuracy <math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>, mean tokens <math id="alg2.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          // Initial probing phase

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow m_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow m_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Minimum trials
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i,\ell}^{(j)}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i,\ell}^{(j)}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Evaluate</span>(<math id="alg2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M},x_{i},t^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M},x_{i},t^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i,\ell}^{(j)}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i,\ell}^{(j)}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CountTokens</span>(<math id="alg2.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M},x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M},x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
          // Compute initial statistics

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{a}\leftarrow\frac{1}{k}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}a_{i,\ell}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{a}\leftarrow\frac{1}{k}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}a_{i,\ell}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{a}\leftarrow\sqrt{\frac{1}{k}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}(a_{i,\ell}^{(j)}-\mu_{a})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{a}\leftarrow\sqrt{\frac{1}{k}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}(a_{i,\ell}^{(j)}-\mu_{a})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}\leftarrow\frac{1}{k}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}t_{i,\ell}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}\leftarrow\frac{1}{k}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}t_{i,\ell}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}\leftarrow\sqrt{\frac{1}{k}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}(t_{i,\ell}^{(j)}-\mu_{t})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}\leftarrow\sqrt{\frac{1}{k}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k}(t_{i,\ell}^{(j)}-\mu_{t})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
          // Compute coefficient of variation

</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CV}\leftarrow\frac{\sigma_{a}}{\mu_{a}+\epsilon}+\frac{\sigma_{t}}{\mu_{t}+\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>CV</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CV}\leftarrow\frac{\sigma_{a}}{\mu_{a}+\epsilon}+\frac{\sigma_{t}}{\mu_{t}+\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CV}\geq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>CV</mtext><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CV}\geq\tau</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">and</span> <math id="alg2.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq m_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq m_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow k+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i,k}^{(j)}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i,k}^{(j)}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Evaluate</span>(<math id="alg2.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M},x_{i},t^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M},x_{i},t^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i,k}^{(j)}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i,k}^{(j)}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CountTokens</span>(<math id="alg2.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M},x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M},x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
            Update <math id="alg2.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{a},\sigma_{a},\mu_{t},\sigma_{t},\text{CV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext>CV</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{a},\sigma_{a},\mu_{t},\sigma_{t},\text{CV}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}\leftarrow k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}\leftarrow k</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l22.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg2.l22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Final sample count
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">23:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}^{(j)}\leftarrow\frac{1}{k^{*}}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k^{*}}a_{i,\ell}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}^{(j)}\leftarrow\frac{1}{k^{*}}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k^{*}}a_{i,\ell}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">24:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{(j)}\leftarrow\frac{1}{k^{*}}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k^{*}}t_{i,\ell}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{(j)}\leftarrow\frac{1}{k^{*}}\sum_{\ell=1}^{k^{*}}t_{i,\ell}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">25:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*},a_{i}^{(j)},t_{i}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*},a_{i}^{(j)},t_{i}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Algorithmic Analysis</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Computational Complexity.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The time complexity of ARISE is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(n\cdot J\cdot\bar{k}\cdot C_{\text{eval}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(n\cdot J\cdot\bar{k}\cdot C_{\text{eval}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the dataset size, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of scaling iterations, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the average sample count per configuration, and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\text{eval}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>eval</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\text{eval}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cost of a single model evaluation. The adaptive termination in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix B Algorithm ‣ ARISE: An Adaptive Resolution-Aware Metric for Test-Time Scaling Evaluation in Large Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> ensures <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{k}\ll m_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≪</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{k}\ll m_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> for stable configurations, significantly reducing computation compared to fixed sampling.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Early Termination.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix B Algorithm ‣ ARISE: An Adaptive Resolution-Aware Metric for Test-Time Scaling Evaluation in Large Reasoning Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> implements dynamic early stopping based on the coefficient of variation (CV) from accuracy and token statistics (line 14). When <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CV}&lt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>CV</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CV}&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, sampling terminates due to sufficient statistical stability. Low-variance configurations converge with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\approx m_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\approx m_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> samples, while high-variance cases automatically expand to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\to m_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\to m_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Adaptive Resource Allocation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The sample count <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> varies per configuration based on observed variance, enabling natural budget redistribution. Stable configurations converge with minimal samples, while stochastic configurations adaptively require more trials, concentrating resources where uncertainty is highest.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experiment Details</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Inference Configuration</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For open-source models, we deploy them using vLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al., 2023</a>)</cite> for efficient inference. Following official recommendations, we configure the generation hyperparameters as follows: Temperature = 0.6, Top-P = 0.95, Top-K = 20, and Min-P = 0. These settings balance between generation diversity and output quality, enabling controlled yet flexible reasoning processes during test-time scaling evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Test-Time Scaling Configuration</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For models supporting variable test-time computation, we evaluate across multiple scaling levels:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effort-based scaling</span> (OpenAI o-series, gpt-oss models): We test <span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">low</span>, <span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">medium</span>, and <span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">high</span> reasoning effort levels, allowing models to allocate increasing computational resources to complex problems.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mode-based scaling</span> (Claude 4 series, Qwen3 series and DeepSeek models): We compare <span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">think</span> mode (with explicit reasoning chains) against <span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">no-think</span> mode (direct response generation). For DeepSeek models, we utilize <span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reasoner</span> (<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">think</span>) and standard <span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">chat</span> (<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">no-think</span>) modes for comparative analysis, with explicit prompts employed to control reasoning length for DeepSeek-R1.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">All experiments are conducted with a maximum token limit of 32,768 for reasoning traces and 2,048 for queries, ensuring sufficient space for complex multi-step reasoning while maintaining computational feasibility. For consistency, we perform five independent runs for each configuration and report averaged results with standard deviations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
